      "dom_id": "question-106798",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:  \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not raining, **then** you can go to the beach.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not raining.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You can go to the beach.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is raining.\n\n- $¬B:$ You can't go to the beach.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you can't go to the beach, then it is raining.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "source-choice-1",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "If you can't go to the beach, then it is raining.",
              "html": "If you can't go to the beach, then it is raining."
            },
